    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Ran into this while testing locally. It appears that if the output directory (`website/stories`) doesn't exist before running the script, it will sometimes generate only one storybook, with the other one failing ([see log here](https://app.netlify.com/sites/instantsearchjs/deploys/63a1c74333215b000b787069#L624)).\r\n\r\nHaving an existing directory first seems to do the trick.\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n    \"website:storybook\": \"mkdir -p website/stories && lerna run storybook:build\",\r\n```",
    "commit_id": "598d4338f6fb75645af834d3ef979c2b48aa6a12",
    "created_at": "2022-12-20T16:24:44Z",
